### Phase 4: SHIP & PRESENT (Polish, Pitch, Demo, Submission, Readiness, Retro, Mentor)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@roomId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@branchId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@slideId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@qaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004
@rowId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005
@mentorToken = sample-mentor-token-uuid

### ==============================================================================
### 1. GITHUB HUB
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Get GitHub Hub Page
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github
Content-Type: application/json

### 1.2 Connect GitHub Repository (supports "demo/demo-repo" for fake client)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/connect
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "repo": "demo/demo-repo"
}

### 1.3 Sync GitHub Repository
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/sync
Content-Type: application/json

### 1.4 Update Branch Purpose and Role
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/branches/{{branchId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "purpose": "Core authentication and JWT flow",
  "role": "demo-safe"
}

### 1.5 Link Tasks to Branch
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/branches/{{branchId}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "taskIds": ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000010"]
}

### 1.6 Update Deployed Application Link
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/deployed-link
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://brackit-demo.vercel.app"
}

### 1.7 Get Freeze Checklist
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/freeze
Content-Type: application/json

### 1.8 Freeze Demo Branch
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/freeze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branch": "demo-safe",
  "tag": "v1.0.0-demo",
  "sha": "a1b2c3d4e5f6",
  "message": "Demo-safe freeze for judge presentation"
}

### 1.9 Dismiss Attention Item
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/attention/NO_LINKED_TASK/dismiss
Content-Type: application/json

### 1.10 List User Repositories
GET {{baseUrl}}/github/my-repos
Content-Type: application/json

### 1.11 Disconnect GitHub Repository
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/connect
Content-Type: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### 2. PITCH STUDIO (Slides, Rehearsals, Q&A)
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Get Pitch Deck & Slides
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/deck
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.2 Generate / Reset Pitch Deck
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/deck/generate
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.3 Add Slide
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/slides
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "TECH",
  "title": "Architecture & Scalability",
  "question": "How did you build it?",
  "content": "Spring Boot 4, PostgreSQL, React 19, and TailwindCSS with zero-config telemetry."
}

### 2.4 Update Slide Content and Pacing
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/slides/{{slideId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Architecture & Resiliency",
  "content": "Spring Boot 4, PostgreSQL, and Flyway with automated fallback circuit breakers.",
  "durationSec": 35
}

### 2.5 Delete Slide
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/slides/{{slideId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.6 Reorder Slides
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/slides/reorder
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slideIds": [
    "{{slideId}}"
  ]
}

### 2.7 Get Judging Q&A Cards
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/qa
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.8 AI Generate Q&A Cards
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/qa/generate
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.9 Add Manual Q&A Card
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/qa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What happens if the external API fails during demo?",
  "answer": "We have an offline fallback cache with pre-warmed synthetic demo fixtures.",
  "category": "TECH"
}

### 2.10 Update Q&A Card
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/qa/{{qaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Updated answer with specific uptime and fallback details.",
  "pinned": true
}

### 2.11 Delete Q&A Card
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/qa/{{qaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.12 Get Rehearsal History & Statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/rehearse
Content-Type: application/json

### 2.13 Record a Rehearsal Run
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/pitch/rehearse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "durationSec": 172,
  "slideTimings": [
    { "slideId": "{{slideId}}", "paceSec": 28 }
  ],
  "feedback": "Smooth flow. Opener was concise, demo transition was well under 30s."
}


### ==============================================================================
### 3. DEMO & VIDEO STUDIO
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Get Demo & Video Studio Page Data
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/demo
Content-Type: application/json

### 3.2 Update Demo Media Links
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/demo/media
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fallbackVideoUrl": "https://youtube.com/watch?v=sample-demo-run",
  "backupRecordingUrl": "https://drive.google.com/sample-backup-recording"
}

### 3.3 Toggle Demo Insurance Checklist Item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/demo/insurance/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000010
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "checked": true
}


### ==============================================================================
### 4. SUBMISSION CENTER
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Get Submission Checklist & Draft
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/submission
Content-Type: application/json

### 4.2 Toggle Checklist Item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/submission/checklist/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000020
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "checked": true
}

### 4.3 Save Submission Draft
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/submission/draft
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "whatItDoes": "[brackit] guides teams through rules, ideation, development, and pitching.",
  "whyItMatters": "Teams lose up to 40% of their build time to coordination friction.",
  "howBuilt": "Spring Boot, React, Vite, PostgreSQL, Flyway.",
  "challenges": "Real-time state synchronization and deterministic freeze detection.",
  "whatsNext": "Multi-room tournaments and judge scoring portals."
}

### 4.4 Verify Submission Links
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/submission/verify-links
Content-Type: application/json

### 4.5 Submit Final Hackathon Project
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/submission/submit
Content-Type: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### 5. READINESS & JUDGE SIMULATOR
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Get Overall Room Readiness Breakdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/readiness
Content-Type: application/json

### 5.2 Validate Simulated Judge Defense Answer
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/readiness/simulate/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "We benchmarked our engine with 500 concurrent operations. Cache hits stayed at 94%, and latency averaged 12ms."
}


### ==============================================================================
### 6. RETRO & PORTFOLIO
### ==============================================================================

### 6.1 Get Retrospective & Time Analysis
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/retro
Content-Type: application/json

### 6.2 Update Retro Answers / Project Decision
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/retro
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "worked": "Trunk-based commits and strict feature freeze 2 hours before deadline.",
  "didnt": "Attempting too many nice-to-have UI animations in early sprint.",
  "change": "Set up automated test coverage before building the core flow.",
  "decision": "continue"
}

### 6.3 Get Public Portfolio Entry
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/portfolio
Content-Type: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### 7. PRE-EVENT PREP & CROWD CHECK
### ==============================================================================

### 7.1 Get Prep Dashboard Data
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/prep
Content-Type: application/json

### 7.2 Toggle Prep Checklist Item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/prep/checklist/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000030
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "done": true
}

### 7.3 Get Track Crowd Check Rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/crowd-check
Content-Type: application/json

### 7.4 Add Crowd Check Row
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/crowd-check/rows
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "option": "AI Document Assistant",
  "likelyCompetingIdeas": "Resume builders, PDF summarizers",
  "collegeOverlap": "High",
  "crowdedness": "HIGH",
  "notes": "Very common theme, hard to stand out unless execution is exceptional"
}

### 7.5 Update Crowd Check Row
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/crowd-check/rows/{{rowId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "crowdedness": "MEDIUM",
  "notes": "Niche focus on medical discharge summaries differentiates this idea"
}

### 7.6 Delete Crowd Check Row
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/crowd-check/rows/{{rowId}}
Content-Type: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### 8. MENTOR VIEW
### ==============================================================================

### 8.1 Get Read-Only Mentor Room Context
GET {{baseUrl}}/mentor/{{mentorToken}}/context
Content-Type: application/json

### 8.2 Ask Question to Mentor
POST {{baseUrl}}/mentor/{{mentorToken}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Should we prioritize adding mobile responsiveness or live webhooks for demo?"
}


### ==============================================================================
### 9. DEV PROFILE ENDPOINTS (spring.profiles.active=dev)
### ==============================================================================

### 9.1 Seed Present Data (Slides, Q&A, Rehearsal, Media, Submission)
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/rooms/{{roomId}}/seed-present
Content-Type: application/json

### 9.2 Add Synthetic Commits to Branch
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/rooms/{{roomId}}/github/add-commits
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branch": "main",
  "count": 3,
  "beforeKickoff": false
}
